{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 369.9, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Fresh observation in new domain not among original four priorities or five tested: explore a different domain category to further validate or extend the generalization pattern, or synthesize findings and prepare for candidate generation consideration.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E085 experiment: view-count principle on building automation HVAC fault codes. Key results: G1 PASS (30≥30 both arms), G2 FAIL (0.70 accuracy vs 0.85 threshold), G3 REPORTING: treatment 50.0% served (15/30), 20% partially_served (6/30), 30% unserved (9/30); control 50.0% served (15/30), 36.7% partially_served (11/30), 13.3% unserved (4/30). Key differentiator: 20% partially_served rate for HVAC matches industrial PLC/SCADA (E084), continuing the gradient pattern across 5 tested domains: lab instruments 0%, medical devices 1%, aviation 10%, industrial/industrial 20%, HVAC 20%, general computer errors 36.7%. This confirms the dose-response gradient where partially_served rate increases as domains become less code-structured. G4 FAIL (14/20 top-arrival vs threshold 17/20). Five of five domains now tested, establishing the view-count principle's generalization boundaries across technical/non-software domains with systematic domain-differentiated classification patterns. Decision: hold - principle generalizes across all tested domains; fresh observation needed in new domain per D083.", "unlogged_changes": 20}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 25, "session": "2026-10-10-003-fresh-observation-in-new-domain-building", "ts": "2026-10-10T00:22:11+00:00"}
